  {
   "id": "g-notes-programRequirements",
   "label": "Additional program requirements",
   "category": "Liberal ed",
   "sourceRef": "program",
   "rule": {
    "id": "r-notes-programRequirements",
    "type": "review",
    "sourceRef": "program",
    "message": "All students must complete the University's\u00a0 Liberal Education requirements.\nCollegiate Requirements:\nAll incoming CLA first-year (freshmen) must complete the First-Year Experience course sequence.\nAll incoming CLA first-year (freshmen) students earning a BA, BS, or BIS degree must complete CLA 3002 or another approved career or internship course (CLA 3101, CLA 3201, CLA 3301, CLA 3896, CLA 3996, or CPSY 3896).\nAll students must complete a capstone in at least one CLA major. The requirements for double majors completing the capstone in a different CLA major will be clearly stated. Students must also complete all major requirements in both majors to allow the additional capstone to be waived. Students completing an additional degree must complete the Capstone in each degree area.\nAt least 17 upper-division credits in the major must be taken at the University of Minnesota Twin Cities campus.\nStudents may earn no more than one undergraduate degree in Developmental Psychology: a BA, a BS, or a minor. Students may combine the BA in Developmental Psychology with the minor in Psychology. CPSY majors may not also earn a second major or baccalaureate degree in psychology. Students also may not earn both an undergraduate degree in Developmental Psychology and a major in Early Childhood (as both are housed within the same academic department). Verify this requirement with your advisor or APAS."
   }
  }
